 <source>Diabetes</source> <volume>52</volume>: <fpage>102</fpage>&#x02013;110, <year>2003</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12502499</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r17"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal">Maclean N, Ogilvie RF: Quantitative estimation of the pancreatic islet tissue in diabetic subjects. <source>Diabetes</source> <volume>4</volume>: <fpage>367</fpage>&#x02013;376, <year>1955</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">13270659</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal">Saisho Y, Butler AE, Meier JJ, Monchamp T, Allen-Auerbach M, Rizza RA, Butler PC: Pancreas volumes in humans from birth to age one hundred taking into account sex, obesity, and presence of type-2 diabetes. <source>Clin Anat</source> <volume>20</volume>: <fpage>933</fpage>&#x02013;942, <year>2007</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17879305</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal">Ogilvie RF: The islands of Langerhans in 19 cases of obesity. <source>J Pathol Bacterol</source> <volume>37</volume>: <fpage>473</fpage>&#x02013;481, <year>1933</year></citation></ref><ref id="r20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal">Bonner-Weir S: Islet growth and development in the adult. <source>J Mol Endocrinol</source> <volume>24</volume>: <fpage>297</fpage>&#x02013;302, <year>2000</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10828822</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r21"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal">Guiot Y, Sempoux C, Moulin P, Rahier J: No decrease of the beta-cell mass in type 2 diabetic patients (Abstract). <source>Diabetes</source> <volume>50</volume> (Suppl. 1): <fpage>S188</fpage>, <year>2001</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11272190</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r22"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal">Clark A, Jones LC, de Koning E, Hansen BC, Matthews DR: Decreased insulin secretion in type 2 diabetes: a problem of cellular mass or function? (Abstract). <source>Diabetes</source> <volume>50</volume> (Suppl. 1): <fpage>S169</fpage>&#x02013;S171, <year>2001</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11272183</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r23"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal">Saito K, Yaginuma N, Takahashi T: Differential volumetry of A, B, and D cells in the pancreatic islets of diabetic and non-diabetic subjects. <source>Tohoku J Exp Med</source> <volume>129</volume>: <fpage>273</fpage>&#x02013;283, <year>1979</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">392812</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r24"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal">Jonas JC, Sharma A, Hasenkamp W, Ilkova H, Patane G, Laybutt R, Bonner-Weir S, Weir GC: Chronic hyperglycemia triggers loss of pancreatic &#x003b2; cell differentiation in an animal model of diabetes. <source>J Biol Chem</source> <volume>274</volume>: <fpage>14112</fpage>&#x02013;14121, <year>1999</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10318828</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r25"><label>25</label><citation citation-type="journal">LeCompte PM, Merriam JC: Mitotic figures and enlarged nuclei in the islands of Langerhans in man. <source>Diabetes</source> <volume>2</volume>: <fpage>35</fpage>&#x02013;39, <year>1962</year></citation></ref><ref id="r26"><label>26</label><citation citation-type="journal">Lorenzo A, Razzaboni B, Weir GC, Yankner BA: Pancreatic islet cell toxicity of amylin associated with type-2 diabetes mellitus. <source>Nature</source> <volume>368</volume>: <fpage>756</fpage>&#x02013;760, <year>1994</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8152488</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r27"><label>27</label><citation citation-type="journal">Johnson KH, O'Brien TD, Westermark P: Medical intelligence: islet amyloid, islet amyloid polypeptide and diabetes mellitus. <source>N Engl J Med</source> <volume>321</volume>: <fpage>513</fpage>&#x02013;518, <year>1989</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2668761</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r28"><label>28</label><citation citation-type=